Just to correct a few misconceptions....

In article <2182@wheaton.UUCP> kroth@wheaton.UUCP (Ken Roth) writes:
>Priest:     ...    Has extra kicking abilities - useful 
>            at low levels since Priests don't use weapons well until they
>            are fifth level or so.  ...

All characters use weapons equally well, after allowing for strength,
weapon bonuses, etc....

>Chr (Charisma):  I don't know the direct effects but it does effect the prices 
>   in the shops and maybe other things like the chance of Elbereth working. 
>   You increase this with rings of adornment. 

Also affects your chances of getting good results from a succubus/incubus.
It does _not_ affect the chance of Elbereth working.

>   3. Sacrifice on a non-co-aligned altar.
>      +1 (if negative luck & not angry god & successful) 
>         success = 25%, experience level 1 and increases such that
>         success = 100% for experience level 6.

This is wrong.  The applicable code is
		    if (rn2(8 + (int)u.ulevel) > 5) {
There is always a chance of it not working, though it's more likely to work
with high experience.

>The minute you eat a pet, every monster on the level will head for you with 
>blood in its eye(s).  That is, you gain an intrinsic: Aggravate monster

Not true.  Aggravate monster does not affect peaceful monsters, and peaceful
monsters are _not_ going to suddenly attack you (as the above implies).

>Your pets will immediately attack kobolds and orcs.  
>A ring of conflict will make them fight anything.

In fact, which monsters your pet will attack depends on how high a level the
pet is at.

>We are pretty sure that you can tame all types of dogs and cats(wargs, winter
>wolves, hell hounds, jaguars, etc.) but we plan to test this idea more. ...

This was once possible but has been changed.  (I don't remember when the change
was added, though.)

>6:  A wand of cancellation will remove the curse from all items in your pack 
>    if you zap yourself with it.  Note, however, that it will also remove all 
>    enchantments and names (i.e. Stormbringer) on all items in your pack, and
>    all intrinsics.

It won't remove intrinsics.

>7:  Having a monster steal your cursed items.  Nymphs will steal cursed armor
